              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "aequor, aequoris — \"the level sea, the sea's surface; a level plain\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ventus nūllus est, et aequor quiētum est. There is no wind, and the surface of the sea is still."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Third declension, neuter: aequor, aequoris n. First any flat surface, then above all the calm, level sea (a word of poetry)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "aequor is built on aequus 'level, even' (EtymDB; Lewis & Short): a level surface, and so the sea when it is calm."
            }
          ]
        },
